DEUTERIUM REFLECTION (RUZIC) ON CARBON
dreflc.nc

     --Version 1.0--
Data are extracted from the old DEGAS' refl.dat file and set up
with a particular angular dependence: 
\begin{equation}
R_{N}(E,\theta) = R_{N}(E,0) \left[ 1 + 0.5 \sin(\theta \pi / 180) \right],
\end{equation}
where $\theta$ is in degrees. An upper limit to $R_{N}$ of 0.9 is enforced.
The data file is precisely
as generated by pmiwrite.web (should be v. 1.6). To make the correspondence
with the original DEGAS model (lrflct1=3, lrflct2=1) complete, a cosine
distribution (internal option in pmiwrite) is used for the reflected angle.

     --Version 1.1--
Fill unused portion of main data table with real_unused and set unused 
fit coefficient for "cosine velocity_vector" to real_undef (pmiwrite v. 1.10).

